// Output: 1, 4, 3, 2
// Explanation:
// 1. Synchronous code runs first (1, 4)
// 2. Microtasks (Promise) run before macrotasks (setTimeout)
// 3. setTimeout callback runs last

// Call stack visualization
function first() {
  console.log('First');
  second();
}

function second() {
  console.log('Second');
}

first(); // Call stack: first() -> second() -> empty
```

questions.backOfCard:
**Explanation:**
• Event loop manages async operations in single-threaded JS
• Call stack: currently executing code
• Microtask queue: Promise callbacks (higher priority)
• Callback queue: setTimeout/setInterval callbacks (lower priority)

**Usage:**
```javascript
console.log('1');
setTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('3'));
console.log('4');
// Output: 1, 4, 3, 2
// Microtasks run before macrotasks
```

**Real World Example:**
Social media post: UI updates (sync), database save (Promise), analytics (setTimeout) - ensures smooth UX.

