**Explanation:**
• Horizontal: multiple server instances (clustering, load balancers)
• Vertical: increase server resources (CPU, RAM, storage)
• Best practices: stateless apps, caching, database optimization, monitoring

**Usage:**
```javascript
// Clustering for multiple cores
if (cluster.isMaster) {
  for (let i = 0; i < os.cpus().length; i++) {
    cluster.fork();
  }
} else {
  app.listen(3000);
}

// Redis for shared sessions
app.use(session({
  store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient })
}));

// Database read/write splitting
const readPool = mysql.createPool({ host: 'read-replica' });
const writePool = mysql.createPool({ host: 'master' });
```

**Real World Example:**
E-commerce platform: multiple Node.js instances behind load balancer, Redis for sessions, read replicas for products, caching, auto-scaling containers during peak shopping.
